    <div class="head"><h2>Why now</h2><p>Three reasons social value has moved from the CSR page to the board agenda.</p></div>
    <div class="bento">
      <div class="tile tile-dark span-4"><h3>Tenders score it</h3><p>Public buyers across the UK weigh social value alongside price and quality. In Wales, public bodies have had new duties to buy in a socially responsible way since March 2026. A credible, evidenced story is worth marks.</p></div>
      <div class="tile tile-dark span-4"><h3>Your biggest social value budget is procurement</h3><p>Every purchase decides where economic opportunity goes. Local spend, prompt payment to small suppliers and buying from social enterprises create more value than most charitable budgets.</p></div>
      <div class="tile tile-dark span-4"><h3>A cheque is the least you can offer</h3><p>Your skills, buildings, customers, networks and people are worth more to a charity than sponsorship. A strategic partnership is also worth more to you.</p></div>
